## Module 4: Commercial Blasting Agents & Selection## 1. Ammonium Nitrate / Fuel Oil (ANFO)

* Characteristics: The most widely used civil blasting agent. It consists of roughly 94% porous ammonium nitrate prills (pellets) and 6% fuel oil.
* Limitations: It has zero water resistance. If poured into a borehole containing water, the prills dissolve and fail to detonate.

## 2. Slurries and Emulsions

* Slurries (Water Gels): Ammonium nitrate dissolved in water droplets suspended inside a fuel gel matrix. They are highly water-resistant.
* Emulsions: Microscopic droplets of an oxidizer solution suspended inside a continuous layer of fuel oil. They have an extremely high VOD, excellent water resistance, and high density, making them suitable for hard rock underwater.

